      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `argument \u003d\u003d \"-w\"` for comparison would include any special characters preceding the `\"-w\"` argument, leading to inaccurate comparison results.\nFor Instance: if argument \u003d `\"\\0\\0\\0-w\"` Generated from ConsumeBytesAsString(), it will not match with `\"-w\"`. Due to this, in some cases the `\"-w\"` argument will not be skipped.\n\n\nAlternatively, we could utilize `(strcmp(argument.c_str(), \"-w\") \u003d\u003d 0)`, ensuring that strings like `\"-whatsHappening\"` are not skipped. Additionally, when converting a std::string to a C-String, any special characters are eliminated before comparison, guaranteeing an accurate string match.",
